B. the actual forced set on subintervals of (1/sqrt13, 1/2) = (0.277350, 0.500000)
   (window sufficiency: forced at a >= 1/sqrt13 forces dmin^2(a=1) <= 13, i.e. 3N <= 31.4,
    so only rings N in {1,3,4,7,9} can occur -- all inside the computed window)
   a^2 in (0.076923, 0.083333) = (a_lo, a_hi) with a in (0.277350, 0.288675)  ->  forced rings [1, 3, 4, 7, 9]
   a^2 in (0.083333, 0.142857) = (a_lo, a_hi) with a in (0.288675, 0.377964)  ->  forced rings [1, 3, 4, 7]
   a^2 in (0.142857, 0.250000) = (a_lo, a_hi) with a in (0.377964, 0.500000)  ->  forced rings [1, 3, 4]
   ==> on the WHOLE open range the forced set contains {1,3,4}; its exact value is
       {1,3,4,7,9} on (1/sqrt13,1/sqrt12), {1,3,4,7} on (1/sqrt12,1/sqrt7), {1,3,4} on (1/sqrt7,1/2).

C. at a = 0.28 (just above 1/sqrt13): forced rings = [1, 3, 4, 7, 9]
   ==> N=7 IS forced at the small end; the v1 claim 'forced set is exactly N in {1,3,4}'
       is FALSE on (1/sqrt13, 1/sqrt7) = (0.277350, 0.378000).  It is true on (1/sqrt7, 1/2).

D. a = 2/5: the 7 cells {0} u N(0) are pairwise STRICTLY forced: True
   chi(T^2) = 7 : the 7-colouring p+3q mod 7 is 0-free on all 18 vectors with N <= 4 : True
   smallest nonzero same-colour vector has N = 7; witness (p,q) = (-3, 1);
   its strict margin dmin^2 = (28/25)+(0)r3 = 1.1200 > 1  (paper's cruder bound (sqrt21-2)*2/5 squared = 1.0672)
   crude check: min same-colour |v|^2 = 21a^2 = 3.36 > (1+2a)^2 = 3.24

E. tangency audit at the lower endpoint.  Take a^2 = 1/13 exactly (a = 1/sqrt13), ring N=1.
   dmax^2 for a tangent pair = 13 a^2 = 1 exactly, so the unit pair exists only at the
   distance maximum, which is attained at a VERTEX of 2V:
   dmin^2 = (0)+(0)r3, dmax^2 = (13)+(0)r3 (should be 13), maximiser z = ((0)+(2)r3, (1)+(0)r3)
   z is a vertex of 2V, so p and q are vertices of the two hexagons, on the tiling's
   1-skeleton.  Under any partition (boundary-ownership) rule such a point belongs to
   exactly one cell, and need not belong to either of the two tangent cells -- so the
   pair is NOT forced, and the criterion must be strict.  Hence the range is OPEN at 1/sqrt13.
   relative maximiser z - v = ((0)+(1)r3, (1)+(0)r3), one of the six vertices of 2V: confirmed exactly
   [checked: the maximiser is one of the six vertices of 2V]

F. upper endpoint a = 1/2 exactly.  Cell diameter is 2a = 1, so a cell contains a unit pair
   only on its boundary: dmax^2 of one cell = (1)+(0)r3 = 1 exactly, maximiser ((0)+(1/2)r3, (1/2)+(0)r3)
   and the maximiser is a pair of opposite VERTICES, so no unit pair lies in the open cell:
   the interior distance set is (0,1), 1 not attained.  Hence a = 1/2 is admissible.
   rings 1,3,4 are still STRICTLY forced at a = 1/2 (spot check on all ring classes): True
   same-colour ring N=7: dmin^2 = 7a^2 = 1.75 > 1, so the index-7 colouring is proper at a = 1/2
   ==> corrected range: (1/sqrt13, 1/2];  for a > 1/2 the family is empty (a cell
       contains a unit pair in its interior), so the statement holds vacuously there.
